WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.768
Today the words have three sounds.

2
00:00:02.218 --> 00:00:06.996
Three sounds is much harder than two. So your child builds the word in two moves.

3
00:00:07.446 --> 00:00:11.943
Move one. Say the first two sounds, and slide them together with no gap.

4
00:00:14.404 --> 00:00:16.227
Move two. Add the last sound.

5
00:00:17.525 --> 00:00:18.487
The word is sat.

6
00:00:19.387 --> 00:00:24.423
Each row on the page shows the two moves. Point to each box as your child says it.

7
00:00:24.873 --> 00:00:29.419
Do the first row together. Your child tries the next rows with you beside them.

8
00:00:29.869 --> 00:00:32.211
Here is the second row, so you can hear it.

9
00:00:36.016 --> 00:00:37.031
The word is man.

10
00:00:37.931 --> 00:00:43.240
Then your child reads the words with dots. Touch each dot, and slide the sounds together.

11
00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:49.364
If a word will not come, go back to the first two sounds. Do not say the word for them straight away.
